From: Rabs9
Subject: [PATCH] board dts: correct the RGMII transmit delay for gigabit ethernet

The shipped device tree sets tx-delay = <12>, which is outside the window this
board carries real traffic in (9-11). Transmitted frames are corrupted, and the
loss climbs with frame size.

It does not present as a network fault. The link negotiates 1000/full, ethtool
reports zero tx_errors, pings reply normally and receive is unaffected - so it
reads as a bad cable, and it survives changing the cable. What actually happens
is that SSH hangs immediately after key exchange and apt stalls partway through
a download.

The corruption is data-dependent, which is why it went unnoticed: a test payload
of one repeated byte passes perfectly, because the low transition density is
within what the PHY tolerates. Real traffic is high-entropy and fails. Any test
must use random data.

Measured loss at tx-delay 12 with random payloads:

     64 bytes    12%
    300 bytes    72%
   1200 bytes   100%

At 9, sustained 1000 Mb/s full duplex with no errors. 9 is the centre of the
passing window rather than its edge.

Applies to: allwinner-device (device-a733-v1.4.8), configs/cubie_a7a/linux-6.6/board.dts
Runtime override without rebuilding: echo 9 > /sys/class/net/end0/device/tx_delay
---
diff --git a/configs/cubie_a7a/linux-6.6/board.dts b/configs/cubie_a7a/linux-6.6/board.dts
index 60dd64f..02e19db 100644
--- a/configs/cubie_a7a/linux-6.6/board.dts
+++ b/configs/cubie_a7a/linux-6.6/board.dts
@@ -2140,7 +2140,13 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
 	aw,soc-phy-clk-en;
 	/delete-property/ aw,rgmii-clk-ext;
-	tx-delay = <12>;
+	/* RGMII tx-delay: the vendor value of 12 is outside this board's working
+	 * window (9-11). At 12 the link negotiates 1000/full and small frames
+	 * pass, but larger frames are corrupted, which breaks SSH, apt and
+	 * every bulk transfer. 9 is the only value with zero loss at any size.
+	 * Runtime override: echo N > /sys/class/net/end0/device/tx_delay
+	 */
+	tx-delay = <9>;
 	rx-delay = <10>;
 	dwmac3v3-supply = <&reg_dc1sw2>;
 	phy3v3-supply = <&reg_dc1sw1>;
